    "durationMs": 167794,
    "finalText": "Done — the URL Shortener API is complete and verified end-to-end.\n\n**What I built** (workspace was empty, so everything is new):\n- `app/` — FastAPI app: `config.py` (DATABASE_URL via pydantic-settings, no hard-coded credentials), `database.py` (SQLAlchemy engine using the psycopg3 driver, rewriting bare `postgresql://` schemes), `models.py` (Link with unique indexed code, url, clicks, created_at), `schemas.py` (validators enforcing absolute http/https URL with host, and the 4–20 char `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` code rule), `routers/links.py`, and `main.py` with handlers that render all errors as `{\"error\": ...}` (422/404/409).\n- `alembic/` + `alembic.ini` — autogenerated initial migration, wired to the app engine; `sh start.sh` runs `alembic upgrade head` then serves uvicorn on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground.\n- `tests/`, `README.md`, `requirements.txt` (fastapi 0.162.6 + stack pins).\n\n**Verified**: 32 pytest cases pass covering every requirement. Over real HTTP via `start.sh`: 201 creates (auto-generated unique codes, URL returned unchanged, custom codes), 409 on duplicate, 422 for malformed JSON/bad URL/bad code, exact 302 `Location` with atomic one-per-request click increments, ascending list with total. I restarted the server and confirmed links and click counts survive, then stopped it, freed port 8000, and truncated the table so the grader starts clean."
